-- title:
--   Proof of Theorem 2, (27): one step of (25)–(26) is a rank-one downdate of YₖᵀSₖ
-- statement:
--   Let $Y_0, S_0 \in \mathbb{R}^{n\times p}$ with $Y_0^TS_0$ symmetric positive definite, and let $Y_k, S_k$ be generated by the recursions (25)–(26). Then for every $k = 1, \dots, p$,
--
--   $$
--   Y_k^{T}S_k = Y_{k-1}^{T}S_{k-1} - \frac{(Y_{k-1}^{T}S_{k-1}e_k)(Y_{k-1}^{T}S_{k-1}e_k)^{T}}{\langle Y_{k-1}e_k,\, S_{k-1}e_k\rangle}.
--   $$
--
--   In words, each step of the recursion replaces $Y^TS$ by its rank-one downdate along the $k$-th column; restricted to the trailing block this is a Schur-complement step, which is what makes the recursion a Cholesky factorization of $Y_0^TS_0$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The step is indexed by the 0-based column `j : Fin p` (the paper's $k = j+1$), comparing `Ys Y₀ S₀ (j+1)`, `Ss Y₀ S₀ (j+1)` with `Ys Y₀ S₀ j`, `Ss Y₀ S₀ j`. The paper's sentence does not repeat the hypothesis; it is the standing hypothesis $Y_0^TS_0 \succ 0$ of Theorem 2, read as symmetric positive definite (`Matrix.PosDef`). No symmetry hypothesis on $Y_{k-1}^TS_{k-1}$ is added.
-- source:
--   Dahl, Andersen, A primal-dual interior-point algorithm for nonsymmetric exponential-cone optimization, Math. Program. 194 (2022), p. 358, §5, proof of Theorem 2, (27)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ExpConeIPM_Secant_Recursion

namespace ExpConeIPM.Secant

open Matrix

/-- Dahl–Andersen, Math. Program. 194 (2022), §5, proof of Theorem 2, (27), p. 358.
If Y₀ᵀS₀ is symmetric positive definite then, for k = 1, …, p (0-based column `j = k − 1`),
Y_kᵀS_k = Y_{k−1}ᵀS_{k−1} − (Y_{k−1}ᵀS_{k−1}e_k)(Y_{k−1}ᵀS_{k−1}e_k)ᵀ / ⟨Y_{k−1}e_k, S_{k−1}e_k⟩. -/
theorem expansion_27 {n p : ℕ} (Y₀ S₀ : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin p) ℝ) (hPD : (Y₀ᵀ * S₀).PosDef)
    (j : Fin p) :
    (Ys Y₀ S₀ ((j : ℕ) + 1))ᵀ * Ss Y₀ S₀ ((j : ℕ) + 1) =
      (Ys Y₀ S₀ j)ᵀ * Ss Y₀ S₀ j -
        (colInner (Ys Y₀ S₀ j) (Ss Y₀ S₀ j) j)⁻¹ •
          vecMulVec (((Ys Y₀ S₀ j)ᵀ * Ss Y₀ S₀ j) *ᵥ unitVec j)
            (((Ys Y₀ S₀ j)ᵀ * Ss Y₀ S₀ j) *ᵥ unitVec j) := by sorry

end ExpConeIPM.Secant
